{
  "description": "You attempt to interrupt a creature in the process of casting a spell. The creature makes a Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the spell dissipates with no effect, and the action, Bonus Action, or Reaction used to cast it is wasted; if a slot was used, the slot isn't expended. Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot: you automatically end a spell on the target if the spell's level is equal to or less than the level of the spell slot you use.",
